---
import BaseLayout from "../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro";
import Header from "../components/layout/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/layout/Footer.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — GLP Index"
  description="GLP Index provides free, private calculators for GLP-1 medications built on published clinical trial data. About our method, sources, funding, and disclaimers."
>
  <Header />

  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="crumbs">
        <a href="/">GLP Index</a>
        <span class="sep">/</span>
        <span class="now">About</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="serif" style="font-weight:500;font-size:clamp(40px,5vw,60px)">
        Built for the <em>questions</em> people actually have.
      </h1>
      <p class="deck" style="margin-top:18px;font-size:18px;max-width:58ch">
        GLP Index is an independent reference for people taking — or considering — Ozempic, Wegovy, Wegovy HD, Mounjaro, and Zepbound. No accounts. No upsell. No marketing data. Just the numbers, with sources.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="longform">
      <aside class="toc">
        <h4>On this page</h4>
        <a href="#what">What this is</a>
        <a href="#not">What it isn't</a>
        <a href="#data">Data sources</a>
        <a href="#method">How we project</a>
        <a href="#funded">How we're funded</a>
        <a href="#updated">Last updated</a>
        <a href="#disclaim">Medical disclaimer</a>
      </aside>

      <article class="body">
        <section id="what">
          <h2 class="serif">What this is</h2>
          <p class="lede-p serif">
            A small, focused reference for people who just got a GLP&#8209;1 prescription — or are thinking about one — and have ordinary, important questions that shouldn't require a doctor's visit or a Reddit deep dive.
          </p>
          <p>
            When someone starts Wegovy or Mounjaro, three questions tend to surface in the first week: <em>How much weight will I actually lose?</em> <em>How much is this going to cost?</em> <em>When do I increase my dose?</em> Each of those has a real answer grounded in the published clinical-trial data — and that data is what GLP Index is built on.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="not">
          <h2 class="serif">What it isn't</h2>
          <p>
            GLP Index is <strong>not</strong> a medical provider. We don't diagnose, treat, or prescribe. We don't run a telehealth practice. We don't connect you to one. We have no affiliate relationships of any kind on the calculator pages — and if we ever do, they will be labelled and excluded from the medical math.
          </p>
          <p>
            The projections you'll see are <strong>averages from clinical trials</strong>. Your individual response will vary — possibly significantly. Nothing on this site is medical advice. Always talk to your healthcare provider before starting, stopping, or changing any medication.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="data">
          <h2 class="serif">Data sources</h2>
          <p>Every projected number on this site traces back to a peer-reviewed clinical trial. We don't model. We don't blend. We don't extrapolate beyond the trial endpoints.</p>
          <ul class="source-list">
            <li>
              <span class="drug">Wegovy HD<small>semaglutide 7.2 mg</small></span>
              <span class="src">STEP UP · Novo Nordisk et al.<br/><a class="cite" href="https://www.nejm.org/doi/10.1056/NEJMoa2501010">N Engl J Med 392:1501 (2025) ↗</a></span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="drug">Wegovy<small>semaglutide 2.4 mg</small></span>
              <span class="src">STEP 1 · Wilding et al.<br/><a class="cite" href="https://www.nejm.org/doi/10.1056/NEJMoa2032183">N Engl J Med 384:989 (2021) ↗</a></span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="drug">Ozempic<small>semaglutide 1 mg</small></span>
              <span class="src">STEP 2 · Davies et al.<br/><a class="cite" href="https://www.thelancet.com/journals/lancet/article/PIIS0140-6736(21)00213-0/fulltext">Lancet 397:971 (2021) ↗</a></span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="drug">Mounjaro<small>tirzepatide</small></span>
              <span class="src">SURPASS-2, SURMOUNT-1<br/><a class="cite" href="https://www.nejm.org/doi/10.1056/NEJMoa2204817">NEJM 385:503 / 387:205 ↗</a></span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="drug">Zepbound<small>tirzepatide</small></span>
              <span class="src">SURMOUNT-1 · Jastreboff et al.<br/><a class="cite" href="https://www.nejm.org/doi/10.1056/NEJMoa2206038">N Engl J Med 387:205 (2022) ↗</a></span>
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p style="font-size:14px;color:#6B655C">
            Dose escalation schedules come from FDA-approved prescribing information for each medication. Drug pricing is updated manually monthly and reflects estimates from GoodRx and named telehealth providers — actual prices vary by pharmacy, location, and insurance.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="method">
          <h2 class="serif">How we project</h2>
          <p>
            The weight-loss timeline takes the published mean percentage loss at each trial week and applies it to your starting weight. We don't apply a personalization model — there isn't one we'd trust. The chart shows the trial average and notes the variance from the published data so you can see where your individual outcome might land.
          </p>
          <p>
            The dose schedule is a deterministic walk through the FDA label, anchored to a start date you choose. The cost comparison reflects current cash, GoodRx, manufacturer-savings-card, and telehealth pricing pulled in the month listed at the top of the comparison page.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="funded">
          <h2 class="serif">How we're funded</h2>
          <div class="callout callout-sage">
            <div class="callout-label">Today</div>
            <p><strong>GLP Index is free and independently maintained.</strong> No advertising. No affiliate links on any calculator page. No paid placements.</p>
          </div>
          <p>
            In the future, we may add affiliate partnerships with licensed telehealth providers — clearly labelled, and never inside the calculator outputs. If we do, we'll only partner with providers that prescribe <strong>FDA-approved, brand-name GLP-1 medications through licensed physicians</strong>. We will not partner with compounding pharmacies selling unapproved formulations.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="updated">
          <h2 class="serif">Last updated</h2>
          <p>
            Trial data: stable since the original publications (we link to peer-reviewed sources rather than restating numbers). FDA prescribing information: checked quarterly. Pricing: refreshed monthly. The data version is shown at the top of every page.
          </p>
          <p style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;font-size:13px;color:#6B655C">
            Current build · <strong style="color:#3F5D52">v.2026.05</strong> · pricing pulled May 1, 2026
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="disclaim">
          <h2 class="serif">Medical disclaimer</h2>
          <div class="callout callout-warn">
            <div class="callout-label">Please read</div>
            <p>The information on GLP Index is for informational and educational purposes only. It is not a substitute for professional medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment.</p>
            <p>Weight loss projections are estimates based on averages from published clinical trials conducted under controlled conditions. Individual results vary based on starting weight, adherence, diet, activity, metabolism, and other factors. The trial populations may not represent your individual situation.</p>
            <p>Drug pricing is for general comparison and may not reflect the price you'll pay at your specific pharmacy. Prices change frequently and vary by location, insurance, and pharmacy.</p>
            <p><strong>If you are experiencing a medical emergency, call 911 or go to your nearest emergency room.</strong></p>
          </div>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-head {
    padding: 64px 0 40px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #E0DAD0;
  }

  .longform {
    padding: 64px 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;
    gap: 64px;
    align-items: start;
  }

  /* TOC */
  .toc {
    position: sticky;
    top: 88px;
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  .toc h4 {
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #6B655C;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }

  .toc a {
    display: block;
    padding: 6px 0 6px 14px;
    color: #3A352E;
    border-left: 1px solid #E0DAD0;
    margin-left: -15px;
    transition: color 0.15s, border-color 0.15s;
  }

  .toc a:hover { color: #3F5D52; }

  /* Body */
  .body { max-width: 680px; }

  .body section { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .body h2 {
    font-family: "Fraunces", serif;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 30px;
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    margin: 48px 0 16px;
    color: #1A1815;
  }

  .body h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }

  .body h3 {
    font-family: "Fraunces", serif;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 20px;
    margin: 28px 0 10px;
  }

  .body p {
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: #3A352E;
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 65ch;
  }

  .lede-p {
    font-size: 22px !important;
    line-height: 1.4 !important;
    color: #1A1815 !important;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
  }

  .body strong { color: #1A1815; font-weight: 600; }

  .body a {
    color: #3F5D52;
    border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, #3F5D52 30%, transparent);
  }

  .body a:hover { border-bottom-color: #3F5D52; }

  /* Source list */
  .source-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
    margin: 24px 0;
  }

  .source-list li {
    background: #FBFAF7;
    border: 1px solid #E0DAD0;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 16px 20px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    gap: 16px;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .source-list .drug {
    font-family: "Fraunces", serif;
    font-size: 17px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #1A1815;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
  }

  .source-list .drug small {
    display: block;
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    color: #6B655C;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-top: 3px;
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .source-list .src {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: #3A352E;
    text-align: right;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .source-list .src .cite { margin-top: 4px; display: inline-block; }

  /* Callouts */
  .callout {
    padding: 24px 28px;
    border-radius: 10px;
    margin: 32px 0;
    border: 1px solid;
  }

  .callout p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .callout-label {
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #6B655C;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .callout-sage {
    background: #E8EDE9;
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, #3F5D52 25%, #E0DAD0);
  }

  .callout-sage .callout-label { color: #3F5D52; }

  .callout-warn {
    background: #FFF7E8;
    border-color: #E8C97A;
  }

  .callout-warn .callout-label { color: #C2410C; }

  @media (max-width: 980px) {
    .longform { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 32px; }
    .toc { position: static; }
  }
</style>
